\(\boxed{
Observations point to a far object with redshift about zero point five. The measured line corresponds to about three point nine micro electron volts. In the rest frame this would be about five point nine micro electron volts. That value matches the hyperfine split of the ground state of the simplest atom (one proton plus electron). This line appears when photons travel through gas where the atoms are not excited and move slowly. Such gas is known as the neutral atomic component of the interstellar medium. Therefore the correct choice is the option describing a medium where atoms move slowly.
}\)
ANSWER: D
